>> scene lankaCourt style=kachni
>> music silence
>> cast ravana at 0.4
>> prop bow bow at 0.56 raw=true
>> title Meanwhile, in Lanka / A Father
They bring him the bow, and nothing else. For once all ten heads are quiet.
>> move ravana to 0.48 in 1.6
>> pose ravana give
>> play hold \{"visual":"lamp","at":0.7,"time":10,"hint":"l5.4","noMeter":true,"cue":"bellSoft","texts":\["l5.5","l5.6","l5.7","l5.8"\]\}
>> pose ravana swing0
>> music dark
>> shake 4
RAVANA: She is the cause. I will go to the grove now and do what I should have done a year ago.
>> enter minister from right to 0.74 in 0.8
>> pose minister namaste
MINISTER: You are a king, and learned in the law. A king does not kill a woman. Turn that anger on the man.
>> pose ravana stand
>> heads \{"voices":\["anger","father"\],"lines":\{"anger":"l5.11","father":"l5.12"\}\}
He turns back from the door. It is the last thing anyone talks him out of.
RAVANA: Bring my spear. The one Maya made. And my armour.
-> END
